\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of related FedRL works. \textbf  {Byz.\ robust}: tolerates Byzantine clients. \textbf  {Variance red.}: uses variance reduction in gradient estimation. \textbf  {Multi-env}: evaluated on more than one environment. \textbf  {Real FL stack}: built on a production federated learning framework (not a custom simulation loop). \textbf  {Shared codebase}: implementation is public and reusable. \textbf  {Defines eval.\ problem}: provides a formal definition of the evaluation setup.}}{6}{table.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
